  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1213 AM CDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nTuesday through Sunday:\n\nHigh pressure remains in place through much of the work week, \ngradually propagating eastward. Occasional low pressure systems\npropagating across northern portions of the Canadian Prairies will\nbring generally light southerly winds, calming overnight.\nTemperatures will gradually rise through the week with highs from\nthe upper 60s to low 70s and lows in the low 40s to upper 40s and\nlow 50s by the end of the week. During the day, light winds will\nallow for a weak lake breeze in Lake Michigan counties.\n\nGoing into the weekend, strong low pressure looks to propagate\nthrough the Canadian Prairies, bringing increasing southerly winds\nand increasing cloud cover Saturday, and the next chances for\nprecipitation Sunday as a frontal boundary from this system \nmoves southward through Wisconsin. Strength and timing of this \nfront still in question, and with plenty of dry air in place \nahead of the front to prevent precipitation from reaching the\nground.\n\nMH",
